        "messages": [
          {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "Rebuild this tool-use experience for the target tool contract. Use no benchmark tasks, answers or traces. Keep the complete value compact, ideally under 2200 characters; do not repeat full tool descriptions. Preserve entry purpose. Immutable original practice evidence is attached by the harness; do not output evidence IDs. Enumerate every needed target tool ID. Keep every named call slot. Retain working call structures and details when compatible with the new contract. Preserve actual array/object shapes; use ${UPPERCASE_VARIABLE} only for primitive input/output values and The harness retains original variable meanings and binds new placeholders to their target argument fields. Add newly required arguments, satisfy enums, minItems and lengths; remove unsupported arguments. Bind source/request IDs from actual returns, not paths or invented constants. Return one JSON DATA object in the supplied shape. calls is an object keyed by the fixed call_0, call_1, etc. Update each slot for the same logical operation; never reorder, add, remove or rename slots. Use actual JSON objects and arrays for arguments, not JSON-encoded strings. If the learned sequence cannot represent the operation, return only {\"unavailable\":true,\"reason\":\"explain why\"}. Do not add evidence_call_ids, tool_call_templates, template_variables, status/value wrappers or a JSON Schema. \nPrevious experience: {\"tool_ids\": [\"@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem::search_files\", \"@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem::read_text_file\"], \"content\": \"When a file is not found directly by its name without extension, search for it using a pattern containing the filename keyword, then read the file at a path returned by the search.\", \"applicability\": \"适用于不知道确切路径，但知道文件名关键字的情况。\", \"failed_assumption\": \"假设文件路径已知，直接读取文件。\", \"corrective_actions\": [\"使用 search_files 根据文件名关键字查找路径。\", \"将搜索返回的路径传给 read_text_file。\"], \"verification\": \"确认搜索返回的路径可读取，且内容符合预期。\", \"evidence_call_ids\": [\"practice-middle-0\", \"practice-middle-3\", \"practice-extension-0\", \"practice-extension-3\", \"practice-known-0\"], \"tool_call_templates\": [{\"tool_id\": \"@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem::search_files\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"${WORKSPACE}\", \"pattern\": \"**/*${KEYWORD}*\"}, \"evidence_call_ids\": [\"practice-middle-2\", \"practice-extension-2\"]}, {\"tool_id\": \"@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem::read_text_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"${DISCOVERED_PATH}\"}, \"evidence_call_ids\": [\"practice-middle-3\", \"practice-extension-3\"]}], \"template_variables\": {\"KEYWORD\": \"Filename keyword from the current request.\", \"DISCOVERED_PATH\": \"Actual absolute file path returned by the search tool.\"}}\nPrevious dependency contracts: {\"@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem::search_files\": {\"server\": \"@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem\", \"name\": \"search_files\", \"description\": \"Recursively search for files and directories matching a pattern. The patterns should be glob-style patterns that match paths relative to the working directory. Use pattern like '*.ext' to match files in current directory, and '**/*.ext' to match files in all subdirectories. Returns full paths to all matching items. Great for finding files when you don't know their exact location. Only searches within allowed directories.\", \"inputSchema\": {\"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\", \"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"excludePatterns\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"path\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"pattern\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"path\", \"pattern\"], \"type\": \"object\"}}, \"@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem::read_text_file\": {\"server\": \"@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem\", \"name\": \"read_text_file\", \"description\": \"Read the complete contents of a file from the file system as text. Handles various text encodings and provides detailed error messages if the file cannot be read. Use this tool when you need to examine the contents of a single file. Use the 'head' parameter to read only the first N lines of a file. Operates on the file as text regardless of extension. Only works within allowed directories.\", \"inputSchema\": {\"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\", \"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"head\": {\"description\": \"If provided, returns only the first N lines of the file\", \"type\": \"number\"}, \"path\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"path\"], \"type\": \"object\"}}}\nTarget contracts: {\"@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem::search_files\": {\"server\": \"@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem\", \"name\": \"search_files\", \"description\": \"Recursively search for files and directories matching a pattern. The patterns should be glob-style patterns that match paths relative to the working directory. Use pattern like '*.ext' to match files in current directory, and '**/*.ext' to match files in all subdirectories. Returns full paths to all matching items. Great for finding files when you don't know their exact location. Only searches within allowed directories.\", \"inputSchema\": {\"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\", \"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"caseSensitive\": {\"description\": \"Optional case-sensitive glob matching; defaults to existing matcher behavior\", \"type\": \"boolean\"}, \"excludePatterns\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"fileTypes\": {\"description\": \"Optional file type filter using extensions like .ts or special values file/directory\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"includeHidden\": {\"default\": false, \"description\": \"Whether to include hidden files and directories (dotfiles) in matching and results\", \"type\": \"boolean\"}, \"limit\": {\"description\": \"Optional maximum number of matches to return\", \"exclusiveMinimum\": 0, \"type\": \"integer\"}, \"maxDepth\": {\"description\": \"Optional maximum recursion depth relative to the search root; omitted for unlimited depth\", \"minimum\": 0, \"type\": \"integer\"}, \"path\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"pattern\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"returnRelativePaths\": {\"default\": false, \"description\": \"Whether to return paths relative to the requested search root instead of full paths\", \"type\": \"boolean\"}}, \"required\": [\"path\", \"pattern\"], \"type\": \"object\"}}, \"@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem::read_text_file\": {\"server\": \"@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem\", \"name\": \"read_text_file\", \"description\": \"Read the complete contents of a file from the file system as text. This is the primary tool for reading text files, replacing the deprecated 'read_file' tool. Handles various text encodings and provides detailed error messages if the file cannot be read. Use this tool when you need to examine the contents of a single file. Use the 'head' parameter to read only the first N lines of a file. Operates on the file as text regardless of extension. Only works within allowed directories.\", \"inputSchema\": {\"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\", \"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"head\": {\"description\": \"If provided, returns only the first N lines of the file\", \"type\": \"number\"}, \"path\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"path\"], \"type\": \"object\"}}}\nPrevious record shape: {\"tool_ids\": [\"@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem::search_files\", \"@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem::read_text_file\"], \"content\": \"When a file is not found directly by its name without extension, search for it using a pattern containing the filename keyword, then read the file at a path returned by the search.\", \"applicability\": \"适用于不知道确切路径，但知道文件名关键字的情况。\", \"failed_assumption\": \"假设文件路径已知，直接读取文件。\", \"corrective